.SS "void csmp::IsoparametricQuadraticLineElement::dN (\fBDenseMatrix\fP< DM_MIN > & DN)\fR [virtual]\fP"
Compute derivatives of interpolation functions at corresponding nodes with respect to the global coordinate system\&. 
.br

.PP
It is assumed that the element is a straight line in space\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The element is used to obtain the global interpolation of the tetrahedron and the interpolation function derivatives at each node are returned into the matrix M of dimensions rows = spatial dimensions x columns = nodes\&. 
.br

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIDN\fP The interpolation-function derivative matrix is returned into the second method argument\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Reimplemented from \fBcsmp::FiniteElement\fP\&.
